        <dc:title>Strategic Feature Selection for Draft Prediction in League of Legends</dc:title>
        <dcterms:abstract>Draft phase decisions significantly influence match outcomes in MOBA games, yet optimal champion selection requires extensive strategic knowledge. We present a machine learning framework as a data-driven innovation strategy for League of Legends draft prediction through systematic feature engineering and algorithm evaluation. Using 86,556 high-level matches, we engineered 156 strategic features across eight categories: Meta, Synergy, Matchup, Bans, Picks, Runes, Strategic, Spells. Through evaluation of 20 algorithms, we identify LightGBM as optimal, achieving 83.1% test accuracy with 92.2% ROC-AUC and minimal generalization gap (0.27%). Feature importance analysis reveals that meta strength (26.3%), team synergy (24.8%), and counter-matchups (20.6%) dominate draft success, while rune and spell selections contribute minimally (6.7% combined). This work establishes empirical benchmarks for draft prediction and provides reproducible methodology for competitive gaming analytics, supporting economic growth and development in the digital sports sector. © 2026 IEEE.</dcterms:abstract>
        <dc:date>2026</dc:date>
        <z:language>English</z:language>
